@startuml arch_session
!include palette.iuml
title What does an agent session load, and when?

actor User as user
participant "Agent" as agent
collections "Instructions" as rules
collections "Skills" as skills
participant "Hooks" as hooks
participant "Subagent" as sub

== Session start ==
agent -> rules : global rules\n(&#126;/.agents/AGENTS.md)
agent -> rules : the project's AGENTS.md
agent -> skills : name and description\nof every skill
opt Claude Code, after a compaction or resume
  agent -> hooks : session_refresh.py
  hooks --> agent : reminder and git state
end

== A request ==
user -> agent : request or /name
agent -> skills : body of the matching\nSKILL.md
agent -> sub : delegate: scout,\ngate-runner or reviewer
note right of sub : fresh context, its own\ninstructions and tools
sub --> agent : brief, gate table\nor findings

== Each tool call ==
agent -> hooks : before a shell command:\nguard_bash.py
hooks --> agent : allow, or block\nwith the reason
agent -> hooks : after an edit:\nafter_edit.py
hooks --> agent : dash report or\nformat notice

legend right
  Solid arrow: a read or a call
  Dashed arrow: the reply
endlegend
@enduml
